WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.632
Now we combine several cleaning steps in a consistent order.

00:00:03.632 --> 00:00:06.562
First, exact duplicates are removed.

00:00:06.562 --> 00:00:12.757
Missing channel values are filled, then channel text is stripped and converted to lowercase.

00:00:12.757 --> 00:00:18.072
Amount is converted to numeric, and conversion failures become missing values.

00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:21.404
Finally, missing amounts are filled with the median.

00:00:22.007 --> 00:00:27.914
Once the table is clean enough for this example, we group by channel and sum the amounts.

00:00:27.914 --> 00:00:35.742
The value of a pipeline is consistency: the same ordered steps can be reviewed, reused, and tested.
